#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:0
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:8
msgid "gpio-control interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"The `gpio-control` interface provides privileged access to all aspects of "
"GPIO pins. For accessing specific GPIO pins with limited scope, see {ref}"
"`The gpio interface <interfaces-gpio-interface>` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"Due to its wide-ranging access, it is a {ref}`super-privileged interface "
"<reference-operations-interfaces-super-privileged-interfaces>`, and as such, "
"is restricted by default. This interface requires modification of its snap "
"declaration for distribution via the Snap Store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:14
msgid "This interface is used for:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:16
msgid "Fine-grained control of GPIO pins (input and output)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:17
msgid "Building custom hardware interfaces, such as LEDs, relays, or sensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:18
msgid ""
"Low-level interaction with GPIO hardware using character devices or sysfs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:20
msgid "**Developer Details**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:22
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no</br> **{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-"
"privileged-interfaces>`**: yes</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:22
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:26
msgid ""
"This interface controls a resource shared by the whole system. Snaps that "
"use it can be installed as parallel instances, but every instance acts on "
"the same system resource and snapd does not coordinate between them. Make "
"sure each instance manages different resources, or run only one instance at "
"a time. See {ref}`Snaps that are unsupported as parallel instances "
"<interfaces-parallel-installs-shared-resources>` for details.."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:29
msgid "**Path Access**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:31
msgid ""
"The `gpio-control` interface grants read-write access to the following paths:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:33
msgid "Sysfs Interface:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:34
msgid ""
"`/sys/class/gpio/` paths for exporting, setting direction, toggling values, "
"and more:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:35
msgid "`/sys/class/gpio/{,un}export`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:36
msgid "`/sys/class/gpio/gpio\\[0-9\\]\\*/{active\\_low,direction,value,edge}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:37
msgid "Additional symlink paths (platform-specific):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:38
msgid ""
"`/sys/devices/platform/\\*\\*/gpio/gpio\\[0-9\\]\\*/"
"{active\\_low,direction,value,edge} `"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:39
msgid "Gpiochip Interface:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:40
msgid ""
"`/dev/gpiochip\\[0-9\\]\\` paths for direct hardware interaction through the "
"_gpiod_ API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:42
msgid "The following UDev rules are applied to enable device access:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:44
msgid "`SUBSYSTEM==\"gpio\", KERNEL==\"gpiochip[0-9]*\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:46
msgid ""
"Requires snapd version 2.41+. `gpoichip\\*` access requires snapd version "
"2.65+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:48
msgid ""
"The following is an example of a snapcraft.yaml configuration for the GPIO "
"control interface, following the descriptive interface reference practice "
"for clarity:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:50
msgid ""
"name: gpio-control-app\n"
"version: '1.0'\n"
"summary: An example snap for controlling GPIO pins\n"
"description: |\n"
"  This snap demonstrates how to use the GPIO Control interface to manage "
"GPIO hardware for custom applications.\n"
"\n"
"grade: stable\n"
"confinement: strict\n"
"\n"
"plugs:\n"
"  gpio-pins-control:\n"
"    interface: gpio-control\n"
"\n"
"apps:\n"
"  gpio-app:\n"
"    command: bin/gpio-app\n"
"    plugs:\n"
"      - gpio-pins-control\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:71
msgid ""
"After building and installing the snap, use the following command to connect "
"the interface manually:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:73
msgid "sudo snap connect gpio-control-app:gpio-pins-control\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:77
msgid ""
"This ensures clarity and aligns with the best practices for naming interface "
"references when using `snap connections`, `snap interfaces`, `snap connect`, "
"or `snap disconnect`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:79
msgid ""
"The source code for the GPIO Control interface is in the snapd repository: "
"[gpio\\_control.go](https://github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/master/"
"interfaces/builtin/gpio_control.go)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-control-interface.md:80
msgid ""
"For further testing details, see: [gpio\\_control\\_test.go](https://"
"github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/master/interfaces/builtin/"
"gpio_control_test.go)"
msgstr ""
